From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:35:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 37/39] spu: loop-to-memcpy/memset distribution off unless
 requested (GCC 9.5 behaviour)

GCC 10 enabled -ftree-loop-distribute-patterns at -O2/-Os.  PSL1GHT MARS
mars_task_module.elf (-Os, linked without libc) failed to link with GCC
16: task_arg_copy loop became a memcpy call.  An explicit
-ftree-loop-distribute-patterns still enables it.
---
 gcc/config/spu/spu.cc | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc b/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
index a8c0d90d9d1..cca9a2597b8 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
@@ -243,6 +243,15 @@ spu_option_override (void)
 
   flag_omit_frame_pointer = 1;
 
+  /* Keep loops that copy or clear memory as loops unless asked: since
+     GCC 10 -ftree-loop-distribute-patterns is on at -O2 and -Os and turns
+     them into memcpy/memset calls.  Much SPU code links without a C
+     library (PSL1GHT MARS kernels and task modules among it) and lives in
+     the 256 KB local store, so an implicit library call is a link failure
+     or a size cost there.  GCC 9.5 had the pass off below -O3.  */
+  if (!OPTION_SET_P (flag_tree_loop_distribute_patterns))
+    flag_tree_loop_distribute_patterns = 0;
+
   /* Functions must be 8 byte aligned so we correctly handle dual issue */
   parse_alignment_opts ();
   if (align_functions.levels[0].get_value () < 8)
